{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1299172-the-inner-crucible-quest-please-read-review","id":1299172,"title":"The Inner Crucible - Quest. Please Read & Review","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-24T05:21:00-07:00","id":1299172,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon6.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> The Inner Crucible - Quest. Please Read & Review","content":"I decided to write this quest when the following excerpt caught my eye:<ul><li>A week\u2019s ride from Kamthahar, a valley conceals the Inner Crucible Monastery. Here the Wyld Hunt houses its forces, and here it returns when the hunt is complete. Sometimes it returns with captives: tainted souls*, Wyld mutants, Anathema, and even inhuman monsters such as demons and Fair Folk may surrender to the shikari and seek the wisdom of the Pure Way. Through hard work, obedience, and purifying rituals, unclean creatures seek a cleaner death, and a place in the cycle of reincarnation.</li> <li>From a preview of Dragon-Blooded: What Fire Has Wrought. Written about Prasad.</li> </ul><br /> <b>An anathematic demon-god</b> <b>sits on</b> a small hill, watching the fields, and the mountains, and the sunset. The mountains are of a brownish stone, here and there covered with bushes. They are not far away, and you can vaguely make out small moving shapes cresting one of them before they are shaded by the mountain\u2019s shadow, cast by the setting sun.<br /> Goat herders?<br /> The Hunt? Had another one been slain, or would you be introduced to a new, ah, companion.<br /> <br /> If they were the Hunt, they should be moving down towards the rice fields, which extended to the mountains base, and take one of the dirt roads to the city.<br /> You have toiled in those fields not too long ago, under the watchful eyes of Old Monk Murugan.<br /> <br /> You can hear the noise of the city behind you, though nothing distinct passed through the tall walls of the city, or the monastery of the Inner Crucible behind it. The thought occurrs to you that you could perhaps listen for something if you try, but you are\u2026 relaxed. The city drones on, and animals and cicadas make noise in the fields not too far away, as the sun continues setting. A while passes, and you hear a tired sight behind you. <i>Is he fidgeting</i>, you wonder?<br /> <br /> \u201cDo you see that?\u201d says a gravelly voice, and you turn towards the source. Arnav Ophris, your\u2026 guard? Captor? Shadow? Watchdog? Friend?<br /> He is clad in fine black armour, crafted from jade found at the bottom of the Dreaming Sea, and at his waist hangs a white scimitar as long as a staff and as wide as a human head, engraved with poems of shimmering demon-gold.<br /> <br /> You turn towards where he is pointing.<br /> \u201cThe shapes?\u201d you ask, focusing on them again, as they exit the shadows, and there you see the gleam of demon-gold, and witch-silver, and the strong colours of jade.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Hunt.\u201d, you clarify \u201cYes, I see them.\u201d<br /> <br /> There is a moment of silence as you both watch the shikari walk out of the shade, being revealed by the light of the sun. There are Fareeha and Nalini Ophris, one clad in green jade lamellar covered in prayers for enlightenment to Sextes Jylis; the other in heavy armour of Malfean brass and demon-gold, forged by an anathema not so long ago.<br /> There is the sorcerer Murtaza, and his sister Nandita, from Clan Burano; and Akiyama Genji, a former Immaculate outcaste who had converted to the Pure Way.<br /> <br /> That would be all of them. They were victorious, it seemed.<br /> <br /> \u201cShould not Rajkumari Burano be with them, and Halfdan Wilding?\u201d Arnav butchers the name, but then, you have never been capable of pronouncing it either. The man frowns, his thick black eyebrows moving closer together. \u201cDid they not leave with them?\u201d<br /> <br /> You squint. The tall northerner is nowhere to be seen, but he might be a mouse in someone\u2019s pocket, or an eagle in flight. The Faceless lunar had turned up about thirty summers ago and surrendered to the monks.<br /> <br /> He had been exemplary ever since, and likeable. He had tilled the fields, and, in time, told stories to the children living outside the monastery.<br /> He had even become a devout adherent to the Prasadi faith, and, under guard, he had held sermons in many corners of the land. For could not all seek the wisdom of the Pure Way, and by humility and service, seek to better their place in the cycle of reincarnation?<br /> <br /> \u201cI think Halfdan was supposed to stay with some members of House Burano, something about sorcery, I think.\u201d<br /> <br /> He nodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd Rajkumari has known him since he arrived, so she would stay to keep an eye on him.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNaturally.\u201d<br /> <br /> Things had been different before, you were informed. The shikari had been colder to their captives, and more demanding, but his actions, and the actions of others like him**, had slowly managed to make them a bit less invasive.<br /> <br /> There were still those amongst the Dragon Caste who demanded that no anathema, tainted soul or demon be allowed to perform any kind of service for the land and it\u2019s people, and that their obedience should take the form of prayers for purification in stone rooms deep in the monastery, not in the open or amongst the populace, where they might spread corrupting influence. They were not as numerous as they had been, and with the Empress gone and the Realm focusing on internal matters, the Rani-satrap had quietly begun employing those incarcerated at the Inner Crucible for various tasks. Always guarded, of course.<br /> <br /> First beastmen and sorcerers, then fae and demons, and upon the gentle insurance of Old Monk Mirugan, Halfdan; and the rare other anathema who could either not escape their guards or who were counted on to not try to flee them ***.<br /> <br /> Perhaps, one day, that would be you. You were anathema, after all, and not likely to escape otherwise. Or perhaps, you were.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What kind of anathema are you?<br /> <br /> <b>&lt;Solar&gt;</b><br /> <br /> <b>&lt;Abyssal&gt;</b><br /> <br /> <br /> And: <b>&lt;What caste?&gt;</b><br /> <br /> <br /> What gender are you?<br /> <br /> <b>&lt;Man&gt;</b><br /> <br /> <b>&lt;Woman&gt;</b><br /> <br /> <b>&lt;Other&gt;</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> * The burden of sorcery or the whispers of the dead were thought to taint mortal souls and place a great burden upon them (in this Quest). Look to Ysyr, ye faithful, and weep.<br /> <br /> ** Such as Kaisuke, the Forsaken who had laid down his life while defending a coastal city from the fair folk, who escaped during the commotion but returned as the gates were breached and fought side by side with the shikari who had captured him.<br /> Or perhaps Thousand Forge Master, who thirty years back had forged artefacts and raised manses that helped the productivity of several coastal regions, before he was slain by a lunar assassin.<br /> <br /> *** Either because they had nowhere to go or because Stockholm syndrome mixed with the social-fu of a demigod can be a bitch. Not everyone can/does invest in Integrity, after all.<br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> sorry for focusing so much on Halfdan, but that should be finished by now. He is just a plot device to explain why the inmates of The Inner Crucible monastery have more freedom in this quest that i assume they do in canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25187,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25187-aspiring-hopeful-hero","user":"Aspiring Hopeful Hero","date":".  Edited to make more clear. 03-24-2019, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25187-aspiring-hopeful-hero","name":"Aspiring Hopeful Hero","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T07:05:18-07:00","id":1299199,"title":"","content":"Abyssal, Midnight<br /> <br /> Other: nongendered. You are biologically male, but since your &quot;death&quot;, your perspective on sexuality and relationships has changed - you still feel empathy, but you do not desire companionship as you once did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 03-24-2019, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T07:36:58-07:00","id":1299206,"title":"","content":"Solar, Dawn, Female","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25189-dagurasu","name":"Dagurasu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T10:38:36-07:00","id":1299267,"title":"","content":"Hello. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> To any readers who have not yet picked, but perhaps would like to do so.<br /> <br /> On the Abyssals (as their book is not published):<br /> I will be using am what we know of abyssals in 3e, how they aspire towards the Deathlords, instead of Oblivion or the UCS,<br /> I will be using what we know of the Underworld in 3e, how it contains many afterlives, and is run through by rivers and seas that separate them.<br /> I will <i>not</i> be using Resonance, but virtue flaws (and try to build them off passions, because ghosts).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25187-aspiring-hopeful-hero","name":"Aspiring Hopeful Hero","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}